# >>> yard init: Docker build context >>>
# Yard builds every lane worker and gate image from this directory as the
# Docker build context, so whatever is not excluded here is copied to the
# daemon on each build. Yard owns the two entries below; the rest of the file
# is yours, and this block is appended once and never rewritten.
#
# .yard/local is Yard's own local state — the store, logs, lane workspaces, and
# a live daemon socket, which is not a file a build context can carry at all.
# .git is large, and it is also the main source of image-digest divergence
# between gates: each gate builds from a fresh detached view whose .git differs,
# so a COPY that reaches it misses the layer cache every time.
.git
.yard/local
#
# Your build output belongs here too, and so does any environment your tools
# built on this host: a .venv made here names host paths in the shebang of
# every script in it, and is broken the moment a container reads it. Yard does
# not know which trees this project has, so these are suggestions — uncomment
# what applies, delete the rest, and add your own:
target/
# node_modules/
# dist/
# .venv/
# <<< yard init: Docker build context <<<
